---
title: "Calculus II"
code: "MTH-264"
category: "mathematics"
credits: "4"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/MTH-263"
corequisites: []
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisite: Completion of MTH 263 or equivalent with a grade of C or better."
---

Continues the study of calculus of algebraic and transcendental functions including rectangular, polar, and parametric graphing, indefinite and definite integrals, methods of integration, and power series along with applications. Features instruction for mathematical, physical and engineering science programs. This is a Passport Transfer course. Lecture 4 hours. Total 4 hours per week.
